-- REFUSED: higher-order (un-inlinable function value).
-- The WHERE binding `is positive` is function-valued and is PASSED AS AN
-- ARGUMENT to `holds for` rather than being directly applied. R3 lowers a
-- function-valued binding only when every use is a direct application
-- (inlined into a code: block); a function value that travels as data has
-- no docassemble variable it could become, so the lowering must refuse it
-- by name. Contrast rodents-and-vermin.l4's `not covered if`, which IS
-- directly applied and therefore inlines.
-- The file itself typechecks: the refusal belongs to `l4 docassemble`.

DECLARE Reading
    HAS
      @desc The measured value under assessment
      `the value` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN g IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`holds for` g n MEANS g n

@export Whether the reading is acceptable, via a passed-around predicate
GIVEN r IS A Reading @desc The reading under assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reading is acceptable` r IF
    `holds for` `is positive` (r's `the value`)
 WHERE
    `is positive` MEANS GIVEN x YIELD x GREATER THAN 0

#EVAL `reading is acceptable` (Reading WITH `the value` IS 7)  -- TRUE
#EVAL `reading is acceptable` (Reading WITH `the value` IS 0)  -- FALSE
